{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>and he was not, for Elohim took him.</b> [He] died, and likewise \"take now my soul\" (Jonah 4:3), \"I am taking from you the desire of your eyes\" (Ezekiel 24:16). And afterward [Scripture] explained what [it] was: \"and his wife died.\" And this taking upon Enoch — there is no mention of plague, nor \"and he died\"; and the reason is what is written in the words of Asaph (Psalms 73:24): \"and afterward [in] glory You will take me\"; and likewise in the psalm of the sons of Korah (ibid. 49:16): \"But Elohim will redeem my soul from the hand of Sheol, for He will take me — selah.\" And the discerning will understand:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {0 "Reading ואחר כבוד as '(and afterward [in] glory),' reflecting the Psalms 73:24 citation; the bracketed 'in' supplies the construct chain from the Hebrew."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:24.457102414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}